{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`. Reuse of a page UUID is exercised only for search pages. The paging code is shared across tool kinds, so I did not treat that as a gap.\n\n- **Same result fields as the originating tool.**\n  - `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` checks `complete`, `search_id` and `matches` on every page. It checks that `instructions` appears only on the first page.\n  - `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` checks `node` and `items` on every outline page.\n  - `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` checks `files` on every listing page.\n  - `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` checks `node.selector` and `text` on every read page.\n- **Text reads return successive portions.**\n  - `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` uses multi-byte text. It concatenates the page texts and asserts the result equals the original, while the underlying contents change between pages.\n  - The source-read test does the same for line arrays.\n- **Listings, outlines and searches return whole entries in original order.**\n  - The search test compares each entry exactly, including `node` `n{count}` and its `excerpt`, across more than one page. It asserts the total count.\n  - The outline test asserts `n{i}` and `kind` for every item across more than one page, and that the item count is `names.len() + 1`.\n  - The listing test asserts the full ordered `n{i}` list for 2000 files, including after a new file is added.\n- **Only a page with a successor includes `next`.**\n  - The loops in the search, outline, listing and read tests end when `next` is absent, and they assert more than one page.\n  - The graph-read test asserts `page.get(\"next\").is_some()` equals `index == 0`.\n  - `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results` asserts that a small result has no `next`.\n- **Reuse returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the same successor.** In `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot`, the file is changed after the search. The same `next` UUID is fetched again and the delivered text is asserted identical, which includes the successor UUID. The outline test also shows the snapshot is retained after the file changes.\n- **Malformed, unknown and other-conversation UUIDs return a tool error.**\n  - The outline test dispatches `get_next_page` with `\"invalid\"` and an all-zero UUID, and asserts both fail.\n  - The search test asserts that a peer session's `get_next_page` on another session's `next` is an error.\n  - `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` asserts an `is_error` result containing \"unknown page\" for a foreign page ID from a populated conversation.\n\nI read the paging implementation in `pages.rs` only to confirm it is shared. `Pages::prepare` builds all pages up front, and `Pages::get` replays them.",
  "references": "1ac80069e6c37d2808f2a07935fa541926528e3931df8b3a2c423e0fed2a9800",
